// Bindings added on AROS, loaded after the default keymap.
//
// Two reasons these exist. AROS reads the keyboard through keymap.library, so a
// binding names whatever character the active layout puts on that key, and the
// backquote that opens the terminal is not reachable at all on a French AZERTY
// keyboard. And AROS loads the Linux keymap, which is entirely ctrl-based, so
// the Command key -- which is what a Mac keyboard has where a PC has nothing
// useful -- is not bound to anything at all.
//
// So the alternatives go on Command, where they collide with nothing and land
// under the thumb that expects them. These are additions: the originals still
// work wherever the layout has the key.
[
  {
    "context": "Workspace",
    "bindings": {
      "cmd-j": "terminal_panel::Toggle",
      "cmd-shift-j": "workspace::NewTerminal"
    }
  }
]
